# Agent Relay — example environment file.
#
# ============================================================================
#  THIS FILE MUST NEVER CONTAIN A REAL SECRET.
#
#  Agent Relay does not ask you for, store, or transmit API keys, OAuth
#  tokens, passwords or GitHub PATs. Authentication is delegated entirely to
#  the external tools you have already logged into:
#
#    * Codex          -> `codex login`   (credentials live in ~/.codex)
#    * Claude Code    -> `claude` login  (credentials live in ~/.claude)
#    * GitHub         -> `gh auth login` (credentials live in gh's own store)
#
#  Agent Relay never reads those credential files and never prints them.
#  Copy this file to `.env` only if you need the non-secret overrides below.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: absolute path to the Claude Code executable.
# Only needed when `claude` is not discoverable on PATH or in the standard
# Windows install locations. Can also be set in the app's Settings screen.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_RELAY_CLAUDE_PATH=C:\Users\you\AppData\Local\Programs\claude\claude.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: absolute path to the Codex executable.
# By default Agent Relay uses the `codex` binary that ships with the
# @openai/codex-sdk dependency, falling back to `codex` on PATH.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_RELAY_CODEX_PATH=C:\Users\you\AppData\Roaming\npm\codex.cmd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: absolute path to the GitHub CLI executable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_RELAY_GH_PATH=C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: override the directory that holds agent-relay.sqlite, worktrees
# and logs. Defaults to Electron's per-user application data directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_RELAY_DATA_DIR=C:\Users\you\AppData\Roaming\agent-relay

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: set to "1" to open Chrome DevTools on launch during development.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_RELAY_DEVTOOLS=0
